---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CANON_PATHS } from "../lib/site";
import { LINKS, linkClass, btnPlan } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const ext = { target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" };

const jobs = [
  {
    kicker: "Your store",
    title: "Morning counter",
    tone: "teal",
    body: "Last night’s orders and what’s on the shelf, from the store you already run. The brief is waiting when you unlock the door.",
    never: "It does not touch 4473, the bound book, or a POS.",
  },
  {
    kicker: "GunSearchAgent MCP",
    title: "Ask Betsy AI",
    tone: "pink",
    body: "GunSearchAgent puts Betsy AI on the bot through MCP. The bot asks what the market searched for versus what you have. Any shop with GunSearchAgent on the site can do this. You do not have to host with Coriolis.",
    never: "This setup is not Betsy. Betsy stays Betsy.",
  },
  {
    kicker: "Coriolis",
    title: "Send it to Coriolis",
    tone: "orange",
    body: "It opens a ticket. A human gates it. No money and no metal move without that.",
    never: "It does not change hosting, DNS, or billing.",
  },
] as const;

const connectors = [
  {
    name: "QuickBooks",
    note: "Books, not the bound book.",
    tone: "lime",
  },
  {
    name: "FastBound",
    note: "Read only. It can tell you what the book says. It never writes a disposition.",
    tone: "sky",
  },
  {
    name: "Facebook",
    note: "Scheduled posts that are already policy-safe. No comments. No ads. No arguing with the timeline.",
    tone: "blue",
  },
] as const;

const jobTone = {
  teal: {
    bar: "from-teal-300 via-teal-400 to-transparent",
    glow: "bg-teal-400/25",
    kicker: "text-teal-300",
    ring: "hover:ring-teal-300/50",
  },
  pink: {
    bar: "from-pink-400 via-fuchsia-400 to-transparent",
    glow: "bg-pink-500/25",
    kicker: "text-pink-300",
    ring: "hover:ring-pink-400/50",
  },
  orange: {
    bar: "from-orange-400 via-amber-400 to-transparent",
    glow: "bg-orange-400/25",
    kicker: "text-orange-300",
    ring: "hover:ring-orange-400/50",
  },
  gold: {
    bar: "from-gold via-amber-200 to-transparent",
    glow: "bg-gold/20",
    kicker: "text-gold",
    ring: "hover:ring-gold/50",
  },
} as const;

const plugTone = {
  lime: {
    chip: "border-lime-400/35 bg-lime-400/10",
    name: "text-lime-300",
  },
  sky: {
    chip: "border-sky-400/35 bg-sky-400/10",
    name: "text-sky-300",
  },
  blue: {
    chip: "border-blue-400/35 bg-blue-400/10",
    name: "text-blue-300",
  },
} as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Grok Bot setup | Coriolis, LLC"
  description="One session. Your Cursor seat. The Grok Bots you name in the consult, configured and trained. $995. We never rent you ours."
  path="/grok-bot-setup"
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.grokBot}
>
  <section class="border-b border-zinc-800/80 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <p
        class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-gold"
      >
        AI Studio
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl"
      >
        Grok Bot setup
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
        The industry is buying chat bots. The retail operators that will survive
        the AI singularity are buying a teammate with a computer.
      </p>
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.grokBotHero)}
        alt="Sample Grok Bot app on a gun store POS, roster of Betsy AI, Support, Website, Facebook, and QuickBooks."
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        class="mt-8 w-full min-w-0 rounded-2xl object-cover ring-1 ring-white/10"
      />

      <div class="mt-10">
        <p
          class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-gold"
        >
          Your seat. Your tools.
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">
          What a Coriolis shop uses it for
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 sm:text-base">
          You do not have to host with us. In the consult you pick the job. We
          connect the MCP that job needs — GunSearchAgent for Betsy AI, plus the
          connectors you already own.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
          {
            jobs.map((job) => {
              const t = jobTone[job.tone];
              return (
                <article
                  class:list={[
                    "group relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#070c14] p-6 sm:p-7",
                    "ring-1 ring-white/5 shadow-[0_18px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)] transition duration-300",
                    "hover:-translate-y-0.5",
                    t.ring,
                  ]}
                >
                  <div
                    class:list={[
                      "absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r",
                      t.bar,
                    ]}
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  <div
                    class:list={[
                      "pointer-events-none absolute -right-10 -top-10 h-40 w-40 rounded-full blur-3xl",
                      t.glow,
                    ]}
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  <p
                    class:list={[
                      "relative text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em]",
                      t.kicker,
                    ]}
                  >
                    {job.kicker}
                  </p>
                  <h3 class="relative mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[1.7rem]">
                    {job.title}
                  </h3>
                  <p class="relative mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-200 sm:text-[0.95rem]">
                    {job.body}
                  </p>
                  <p class="relative mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
                    {job.never}
                  </p>
                </article>
              );
            })
          }

          <article
            class:list={[
              "group relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#070c14] p-6 sm:p-7",
              "ring-1 ring-white/5 shadow-[0_18px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)] transition duration-300",
              "hover:-translate-y-0.5",
              jobTone.gold.ring,
            ]}
          >
            <div
              class:list={[
                "absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r",
                jobTone.gold.bar,
              ]}
              aria-hidden="true"
            />
            <div
              class:list={[
                "pointer-events-none absolute -right-10 -top-10 h-40 w-40 rounded-full blur-3xl",
                jobTone.gold.glow,
              ]}
              aria-hidden="true"
            />
            <p
              class:list={[
                "relative text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em]",
                jobTone.gold.kicker,
              ]}
            >
              Connectors
            </p>
            <h3 class="relative mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[1.7rem]">
              The systems you already live in
            </h3>
            <p class="relative mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-200 sm:text-[0.95rem]">
              Same session if that is the one job. Later, tickets:
            </p>
            <ul class="relative mt-5 grid gap-3">
              {
                connectors.map((c) => {
                  const p = plugTone[c.tone];
                  return (
                    <li
                      class:list={[
                        "rounded-xl border px-4 py-3",
                        p.chip,
                      ]}
                    >
                      <p class:list={["text-sm font-semibold", p.name]}>
                        {c.name}
                      </p>
                      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
                        {c.note}
                      </p>
                    </li>
                  );
                })
              }
            </ul>
            <p class="relative mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
              Connectors you already own. We do not sell you the connector.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        Coriolis already runs this way. Grok Bot is xAI’s agent: it has its own
        computer, it signs into the tools you already use, and it keeps working
        when you close the laptop. We will not rent you our seat. We will sit
        with you for three hours, configure the Grok Bots you name in the
        consult on the Cursor account you buy, write the rules, connect the MCP
        you already own, and train the owner or manager who will live with them.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href={withBase("contact")} class={btnPlan}>Talk to Coriolis</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-zinc-800/80 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">
        You buy the seat. We configure it.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        Grok Bot is included on these plans, billed by Cursor / xAI, not
        by us:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-zinc-300">
        <li>Cursor Teams Premium — $120 per seat per month</li>
        <li>Cursor Ultra — $200 per month</li>
        <li>SuperGrok Heavy — $300 per month</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        Those prices are theirs (<a href={LINKS.xaiBot} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >https://x.ai/bot</a
        >). Buy one before the session. Sign in with that account. We configure
        on your seat.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
        Cursor’s Terms of Service, section 1.5(iii), bar anyone from renting,
        leasing, lending, or selling the service. We will not put you on a
        Coriolis Ultra box and call it a product. If someone offers you “our
        Grok Bot” as a subscription, they are selling you a seat they do not
        own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-zinc-800/80 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">What $995 is</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        One time. Not a monthly SKU. $995 is the session, not a unit of bots.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        Three hours, on your seat:
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-4 max-w-3xl list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-zinc-300">
        <li>
          Consult. Which bots. What they are for, what they must never do, who
          owns them.
        </li>
        <li>
          Configure. Names, rules, the MCP connectors you already have. We do
          not sell you connectors. Named bots you pick in this consult can ship
          in the session.
        </li>
        <li>
          Train. The owner or manager sits in the session and leaves able to
          run them.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        Then 30 days of async support on the bots from that session. Email and
        tickets. Not 24/7. Not a helpdesk for the rest of the company.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
        After 30 days, anything else is a ticket. Joel gates it. It is billed.
        There is no retainer. Later bots are tickets.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-zinc-800/80 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">What it is not</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        <p>
          It is not a Coriolis product. It is a setup session for a product you
          buy from Cursor and xAI.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is not Grok Bot 24/7 support from us. The bots can work around the
          clock. We do not.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is not a way around a seat. No shared login. No “we host it for
          you.”
        </p>
        <p>It is not 4473. It is not a POS. FastBound is read only.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">After the session</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        You leave with the named Grok Bots you picked in the consult, on your
        account, with rules you approved, and a person in the building who can
        steer them. Later bots are tickets, not a package we invented.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href={withBase("contact")} class={btnPlan}>Talk to Coriolis</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-500">
        Grok Bot is a product of xAI, available through Cursor. Marks of their
        owners. Coriolis, LLC configures on the client’s seat. We are not
        affiliated with xAI or Anysphere beyond that work. Prices for Cursor
        Teams Premium, Cursor Ultra, and SuperGrok Heavy are set by them and
        can change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
